# multiple_images WITH box memory, on the slow per-scene curriculum and the 0.3
# coverage cutoff (2026-09-25). Stride 3, not 1: at stride 1 the three frames are
# 0.25 m apart and nearly identical, which is why the first stack3 under-learned its
# image input (0.046 action delta vs 0.23-0.32 for the others). Note the batch size
# still scales down with K (64 // 3 -> 16) to fit memory; that remains a confound
# against the K=1 arms and should be stated with any result.
ENCODER=dinov2
IMGFIX=1
FRAMESTACK=3
FRAMESTRIDE=3
BOXMEM=5
BOXMEMAGG=mean
COLLAHEAD=0.7
CURTHRESH=0.75
CURMINEP=100
CURNOTCH=0.25
CURPERSCENE=1
# Coverage rule (2026-09-25, Joana): terminate below 0.4, graded cost below 0.7.
# COH raised 10 -> 50 so the cost is felt: 50 x (0.7 - cov) x 0.01 = 0.10/step at
# cov 0.5, 0.15 at 0.4. At the base weight of 10 it was 0.02/step -- symbolic.
COHTERM=0.4
COHTAU=0.7
COH=50
GPUS=4
